Themes
------

Teal is Osmium's own palette. The other themes take their colours and their
names from the community colour schemes they are named after, so that someone
who already uses one recognises it here. Osmium is not affiliated with,
endorsed by or connected to any of these projects, and each name belongs to the
project that made it.

  Dracula      by Zeno Rocha and contributors, MIT licensed.
               DRACULA is a registered trademark of Zeno Rocha
               (US Reg. No. 6306339) for colour-scheme software. Used here to
               name that project's palette, not as a mark of Osmium's own.
  Nord         by Sven Greb (Arctic Ice Studio) and contributors, MIT licensed.
  Catppuccin   by the Catppuccin organisation and contributors, MIT licensed.
  Solarized    by Ethan Schoonover, MIT licensed.
  Tokyo Night  after the Visual Studio Code theme by enkia.
  Gruvbox      after the colour scheme by Pavel Pertsev (morhetz).
  Rosé Pine    after the colour scheme by the Rosé Pine maintainers.
  Everforest   after the colour scheme by sainnhe.
  Kanagawa     after the colour scheme by rebelot.

Each theme in Osmium is three colours — a primary, an inactive tone and an
accent — taken from the published palette of the scheme it names.


